    "/itineraryStops/11/whyOnRoute": {
      "source_en": "The cruise-terminal return is the day's hard constraint. Dropping off at about 17:00 — eight hours after pickup — leaves a real buffer before the all-aboard times most Busan port calls use, and the guide adjusts the running order on the day if your ship sails unusually early."
    },
    "/itineraryStops/11/description": {
      "source_en": "The vehicle leaves the Yongdusan / Gwangbok-ro pickup point at about **16:45** and drives back through central Busan to **the same terminal you were collected from**, arriving at roughly **17:00** — about **8 hours** after pickup.\n\nThat leaves a comfortable buffer before the all-aboard times most Busan cruise calls use. If your ship sails unusually early, tell the guide at morning pickup: the running order is adjusted on the day, usually by trimming the Songdo and Yongdusan stops."
    }
